@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1. Queue a video for processing (returns immediately — 202).
# The background worker (`python -m workers.video_processor`) must be
# running separately to actually pick this job up and process it.
# Replace with any real YouTube URL (watch, youtu.be, or /shorts also work).
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID_HERE"
}

### 2. Poll processing status (PENDING -> ... -> READY / FAILED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/1

### 2b. Retry a failed (or re-run a completed) video's processing
POST {{baseUrl}}/videos/1/retry

### 3. Get the full stored, timestamped transcript (only once status=READY)
GET {{baseUrl}}/videos/1/transcript

### 4a. Raw search — hybrid (keyword + fuzzy + semantic), no LLM call
POST {{baseUrl}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "video_id": 1,
  "query": "AI replacing programmers",
  "top_k": 5,
  "mode": "hybrid"
}

### 4b. Raw search — exact phrase (quoted), lexical match prioritized
POST {{baseUrl}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "video_id": 1,
  "query": "\"OpenAI\"",
  "top_k": 10,
  "mode": "hybrid"
}

### 4c. Raw search — semantic only
POST {{baseUrl}}/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "video_id": 1,
  "query": "OpenAI",
  "top_k": 10,
  "mode": "semantic"
}

### 5. Ask — normal question, grounded answer with real timestamps
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "video_id": 1,
  "question": "What do they say about AI replacing programmers?"
}

### 6. Ask — find-all query (every mention, deduplicated, each cited)
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "video_id": 1,
  "question": "Find every time they mention OpenAI."
}
